This project uses a mixed licensing strategy. Different components are
licensed under different open-source licenses:

1. Media Engine (packages/neko-engine/)
   Licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License v3.0 or later.
   See LICENSE-LGPL for the full license text.
   See LICENSE-GPL for the GNU General Public License v3.0 text
   (incorporated by reference in the LGPL).

2. Shared Libraries (packages/neko-types/, packages/neko-client/, packages/neko-proto/)
   Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
   See LICENSE-APACHE for the full license text.

3. VSCode Extensions and All Other Packages
   Licensed under the MIT License.
   See LICENSE-MIT for the full license text.

Each package's license is also specified in its package.json or Cargo.toml file.
When in doubt, refer to the license field of the specific package you are using.

Additionally, please review:
- ETHICS.md    — Ethical use guidelines (community expectations, not license terms)
- TRADEMARK.md — Trademark policy for the Neko Suite brand and module names
